# The games are single HTML files, and their tests parse them by string offsets with `\n` markers --
# `extractFunction('makeHiScores', 'return { ... };\n}')` and the vm slices in every game's test folder.
# Git's autocrlf writes CRLF into the working tree on Windows, so those markers stop matching and the
# tests fail locally while passing in CI on Linux. It also silently broke byte-identity between the
# shared snippets: Ludo's copy of the back-button block diverged from the other eight by line endings
# alone, which no grep could see.
#
# Pinning LF everywhere makes the working tree match what git stores, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
